# 🧠 Lab 10 – Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) for Time-Series Forecasting

> **Machine Learning Laboratory** | Building a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) model for electricity demand forecasting using deep learning.

---

## 📖 Overview

Time-series forecasting plays a vital role in predicting future values based on historical observations. In this laboratory, a **Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP)** is implemented to forecast electricity demand using the preprocessed **AEP Hourly Electricity Demand** dataset prepared in previous laboratories.

The MLP model learns nonlinear relationships from historical time-series windows and predicts future demand values. The laboratory demonstrates the complete deep learning workflow, including data loading, model construction, training, validation, checkpointing, prediction, and performance evaluation.

The laboratory consists of a single Jupyter notebook implementing the complete forecasting pipeline.

---

## 🎯 Learning Outcomes

After completing this laboratory, students will be able to:

- Understand the workflow of deep learning for time-series forecasting
- Prepare sequential input windows for neural networks
- Build an MLP architecture using TensorFlow/Keras
- Configure optimizers, loss functions, and evaluation metrics
- Train and validate deep learning models
- Use callbacks for checkpointing and monitoring training
- Generate predictions on unseen test data
- Evaluate forecasting performance using regression metrics
- Interpret forecasting results for energy demand prediction

